---
name: traverse
description: Conduct one bp3 quest from the main session — read state with bp3 q r, dispatch the one step that state calls for, re-read, until the quest is terminal or a human decision is owed.
---

# Traverse

Use when a human in a bp3-enabled repo invokes this skill by
name (`/traverse <quest>`, `$traverse <quest>`) or asks to "traverse",
"run", or "keep going on" a named quest until it lands or
blocks. One quest per traverse. One output: step dispatches
through `bp3 q`, ending in a traverse report — what reached
`exp_fin`, what is blocked, and what human decision is owed
next. Finish lines have report words: `exp_fin` names an exp
whose state is `landed` (its `land` edge taken); `quest_fin`
names quest promotion to master, the only owner-gated finish
line. The FSM states stay `landed`; `exp_fin`/`quest_fin`
name the finish lines in reports, never new edges.

Use `quest` instead to frame a new quest. Use `using-bp3`
instead for a single state operation by hand (one handoff, one
grade, recovery after a dead session). Use
`red-ink-quest-landing-demo` instead when the quest is done and the
human wants the landing writeup. A design under review is
`red-ink`'s job, not a traverse.

## Conductor rule

This skill is the conductor: it owns the loop and nothing
else. It reads state, dispatches the one step the state calls
=== traverse-no-human ===
---
name: traverse-no-human
description: Run several bp3 quests with no human present using the traverse conductor — fleet preflight, park blocked work in the inbox, and end with the check-in report; never attests, never pages, never promotes.
---

# Traverse, no human

Use when a human in a bp3-enabled repo invokes this skill
by name (`/traverse-no-human <quest>...`,
`$traverse-no-human`) or asks to run quests unattended,
overnight, or in a queue with no human present. Several
quests may be named; a Run budget may be stated. One
output: the check-in report (step 5). For one quest with a
human present, use `traverse` instead.

`/traverse-no-human <quest>...` means `/traverse <quest>` per
quest, in queue order, under the no-human rails below. Follow
the canonical `traverse` skill (`skills/traverse/SKILL.md`)
procedure and rules as written there — read state with
`bp3 q r`, dispatch the one step that state calls for,
